===============
Short version
===============
Open hangtime U2 in a hexeditor. Look at 
4048 + (3x 0b4e) = 6232  (0b4e is the highest sound i found in source/speech.asm etc.)

u2 0x6232 = 00 f6 62 00 f6 86 00 f6 98 ffffffff..This is the end of the sound call table pointers.

It means there are three sound headers at:
00 f6 62 
00 f6 86 
00 f6 98

This is a sound header:

01 05 00 00 07 05 6F 00 00 01 [05 34 C7 78] 01 00 [AF] 00  (Block 1 is the location, block 2 is no. of frames.)

Find a free spot in U2 rom, i choose 003a00 and 003a20 for ease of use.
Put the sound header as shown above there, and point to your .DAT file. I extracted them from MK2 U roms.
Edit block 1 [05 34 c7 78] to point to your extracted .dat and block 2 for the number of frames.
You can see the mk2 source for a sound call, follow the tables & pointers for it to extract it.

